urvivor testimony caused  major conflicts which boss cohn will  talk about it is sad but true that her  last years in israel were not happy ones  our bach to put it mildly was not an  easy person to get along with and i  sense that in her last years she felt a  great deal of bitterness and frustration  and so to return to what i said earlier  in conclusion  we are not only here to talk about an  important woman  but we're also here to right or wrong  and i would like to end this talk by  quoting something of parrot says that  auerbach repeated in 1945  when surveying the rubble of warsaw she  thought back to the legacy  of this great tribune of modern  yiddishkeit who had once sought to  inspire a new jewish culture in poland  in eastern europe anchored in both  jewish tradition and european humanism  and i used anita norwich's translation  from her book discovering exile console  my people it needs consolation  strengthen its heart shore up its spirit  don't be the wind that puts out the  flame  instead pour oil intend the wick because  night is poison and despair  death console my people it needs  consolation  thank you  [Applause]  [Music]  you
 

